WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.839
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:15.936
Unit thirty-four: Phrasal Verbs (basic). Today you will use common two-word verbs in everyday English.

4
00:00:16.236 --> 00:00:18.796
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:23.001
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.630
Get up.

7
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:27.372
Get up means to leave your bed.

8
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:29.333
I get up at six.

9
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:32.244
Your turn. Say: Get up.

10
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.683
Get up.

11
00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:37.313
Turn on.

12
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:41.106
Turn on means to start a machine or a light.

13
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:43.182
Please turn on the light.

14
00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:45.855
Your turn. Say: Turn on.

15
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.585
Turn on.

16
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.049
Turn off.

17
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.781
Turn off means to stop a machine or a light.

18
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.675
Turn off the TV.

19
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:59.506
Your turn. Say: Turn off.

20
00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.217
Turn off.

21
00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:05.031
Look for.

22
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:08.214
Look for means to try to find something.

23
00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:10.398
I am looking for my keys.

24
00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:13.508
Your turn. Say: Look for.

25
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:17.275
Look for.

26
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:18.820
Put on.

27
00:01:19.817 --> 00:01:21.689
Put on means to wear clothes.

28
00:01:22.283 --> 00:01:23.482
Put on your coat.

29
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.631
Your turn. Say: Put on.

30
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:30.328
Put on.

31
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:32.142
Take off.

32
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.219
Take off means to remove clothes.

33
00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:37.236
Take off your shoes.

34
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.421
Your turn. Say: Take off.

35
00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:44.036
Take off.

36
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:45.401
Give up.

37
00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:48.323
Give up means to stop trying.

38
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:50.162
Never give up!

39
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.124
Your turn. Say: Give up.

40
00:01:55.967 --> 00:01:56.736
Give up.

41
00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.508
Come back.

42
00:01:59.517 --> 00:02:01.412
Come back means to return.

43
00:02:02.017 --> 00:02:03.157
Come back soon.

44
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.704
Your turn. Say: Come back.

45
00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.568
Come back.

46
00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:15.064
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.917 --> 00:02:18.999
Visal, what time do you get up? Note the two words.

48
00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:29.428
I get up at six. Get up is a phrasal verb. It is a verb with a small word, like up or off. The meaning is often different from the single words.

49
00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.808
Can we separate them?

50
00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:45.643
Some can be separated: Turn the light on. Turn it on. But not turn on it. If the object is a pronoun, it goes in the middle. Others cannot be separated: look for, get up.

51
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.204
How should I learn them?

52
00:02:49.317 --> 00:03:01.349
Learn them in context. Put on your coat. Take off your shoes. Don't give up! Come back soon. Make a small list and use each one in a sentence of your own.

53
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.989
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:09.206
Grammar focus: Phrasal verbs: verb plus particle.

55
00:03:09.506 --> 00:03:10.693
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.383 --> 00:03:12.826
Please turn on the light.

57
00:03:13.717 --> 00:03:15.205
I get up at six.

58
00:03:16.117 --> 00:03:17.234
Don't give up!

59
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:26.625
A phrasal verb is a verb plus a small word. Some can be separated (turn it on) and some cannot (look for). A pronoun object goes in the middle.

60
00:03:27.383 --> 00:03:30.372
Be careful! Don't say: Please turn on it.

61
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.344
Say: Please turn it on.

62
00:03:34.644 --> 00:03:36.307
A pronoun goes in the middle.

63
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.567
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:41.890
Two-Word Verbs.

65
00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:44.352
I get up at six and put on my uniform.

66
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:47.773
Please turn on the light and turn off the TV.

67
00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:51.556
I am looking for my keys, but I can't find them.

68
00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.613
Take off your shoes before you come in.

69
00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.692
Don't give up, and come back tomorrow.

70
00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:02.813
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.139
Please blank the light.

72
00:04:05.439 --> 00:04:08.941
A, turn on. B, turn at. C, turn in.

73
00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.616
The answer is A: turn on.

74
00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.494
It is cold. blank your coat.

75
00:04:17.794 --> 00:04:20.972
A, Put on. B, Take off. C, Give up.

76
00:04:24.533 --> 00:04:26.312
The answer is A: Put on.

77
00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.660
'Give up' means blank.

78
00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.788
A, stop trying. B, start. C, return.

79
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:38.298
The answer is A: stop trying.

80
00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.066
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:41.366 --> 00:04:45.438
A, Turn on it.. B, Turn it on.. C, Turn on it please it..

82
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.522
The answer is B: Turn it on..

83
00:04:52.683 --> 00:04:55.925
According to the reading, what is the writer looking for?

84
00:04:56.225 --> 00:04:59.995
A, the keys. B, the coat. C, the shoes.

85
00:05:03.533 --> 00:05:05.544
The answer is A: the keys.

86
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:09.920
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:10.783 --> 00:05:13.154
Write two sentences with phrasal verbs.

88
00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:23.415
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:23.715 --> 00:05:35.440
I get up at six o'clock and put on my uniform. Then I turn on the radio. These are phrasal verbs. A phrasal verb has a verb and a small word, and the meaning is special.

90
00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.334
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:43.538
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and phrasal verbs: verb plus particle.

92
00:05:43.838 --> 00:05:48.266
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

93
00:05:48.566 --> 00:05:51.486
See you in Unit thirty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:05:51.786 --> 00:05:55.530
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

